The Commission seeks to contract the design of methodologies and the development of new means for tracking research results that occur after the contractual period of the EU-funded projects has ended, in this way enriching and complementing its existing project results repositories.
In order to meet this objective, the Commission seeks to contract the following tasks:
1. design of a methodology for tracking research results;
2. setting up a repository of data sources and collection of data;
3. analysis of and reporting on the collected data;
4. training of Commission staff.
The scope is a portfolio of projects funded under the FP7 ‘Cooperation’ specific programme.
